1. Bash 
= Bash stands for bourne Again Shell .

it is the most commanly used shell in Linux systems that allow users to
interact with the operating system through commands.


2. Bash Script
= A Bash Script is a text file containing multiple Linux commands that
are executed automatically one after another.

# Extension
= .sh

# Bash script
= #!/bin/bash


3. Shebang
= The shebang is always written on the first line of a Bash script.
#!/bin/bash
Without the shebang, Linux may not know which shell should run
 the script.


4. First Bash Script

